          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What is called
            %em topological
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            is a collection of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology
            theories whose cocycles in degree 0 on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            may be represented by pairs of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            modulo a certain equivalence relation.
          %p
            The following is the quick idea. For a detailed introduction see
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Topological+K-Theory"} Introduction to Topological K-Theory
          %p
            First, recall that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            then a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \to X
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            which vary over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            in a controlled way. Explicitly this means that there exits an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+cover"} open cover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            (the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank+of+a+vector+bundle"} rank
            of the vector bundle) and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi k
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi U
                        %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \times k^n \to V|_{U_i}
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i
            which is fiberwise a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
          %p
            Vector bundles are of central interest in large parts of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Weil+theory"} Chern-Weil theory
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+theory"} cobordism theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Vect
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ∼
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect(X)_{/\sim}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
            of vector bundles over a given space is in general hard to analyze. One reason for this is that these are classified in degree-1
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+cohomology"} nonabelian cohomology
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in the (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nonabelian+group"}> nonabelian
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+linear+group"} general linear group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(n,k)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+theory"} cohomology theory
          %p
            To that end, observe that all natural operations on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            generalize to vector bundles by applying them
            = succeed "-wise." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum+of+vector+bundles"} direct sum of vector bundles
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitney+sum"} Whitney sum
            operation. This operation gives the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Vect
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ∼
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect(X)_{/\sim}
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
            of vector bundles the structure of an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-group"} semi-group
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"}> monoid
            )
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo ∼
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Vect(X)_{/\sim},\oplus)
          %p
            Now as under direct sum the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            of vector spaces adds, similarly under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum+of+vector+bundles"} direct sum of vector bundles
            their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank"} rank
            adds. Hence in analogy to how one passes from the additive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-group"} semi-group
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"}> monoid
            ) of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
            to the additive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            by adjoining formal additive inverses, so one may adjoin formal additive inverses to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo ∼
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Vect(X)_{/\sim},\oplus)
            = succeed "\u201D)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group+of+a+commutative+monoid"} Grothendieck group of a commutative monoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mo +
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V_+,V_-)
            of vector bundles (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/virtual+vector+bundles"}> virtual vector bundles
            ”), and then
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotienting
            out the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mo +
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∼
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mo +
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi W
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mo −
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (V_+, V_-) \sim (V_+ \oplus W , V_- \oplus W)
          %p
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo ∼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \in Vect(X)_{/\sim}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
            is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            with group operation given on representatives by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mo +
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi V
                  %msub
                    %mo ′
                    %mo +
                  %mo ,
                  %mi V
                  %msub
                    %mo ′
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mo +
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi V
                  %msub
                    %mo ′
                    %mo +
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mo −
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi V
                  %msub
                    %mo ′
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [V_+, V_-] \oplus [V'_+, V'_-] \coloneqq (V_+ \oplus V'_+, V_- \oplus V'_-)
          %p
            and with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse"} inverse
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mo +
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [V_+,V_-]
            given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mo +
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mo −
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \-[V_+, V_-] = [V_-, V_+]
                  \\,.
          %p
            This
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            obtained from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Vect
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo ∼
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Vect(X)_{/\sim}, \oplus)
            is denoted
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X)
            and often called
            %em the K-theory
            of the space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"} Alexander Grothendieck
            = succeed "," do
              %em Klasse
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
            of (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
            of) vector bundles.
          %p
            This simple construction turns out to yield remarkably useful groups of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariants"} invariants
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
            have fairly elementary proofs in terms of topological K-theory, for instance the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+invariant+one"} Hopf invariant one
            problem (
            %a{:href => "#AdamsAtiyah66"}> Adams-Atiyah 66
            ).
          %p
            One defines the “higher” K-groups of a topological space to be those of its higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+suspensions"} reduced suspensions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi n
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  K^{-n}(X) = K(\Sigma^n X)
                  \\,.
          %p
            The assignment
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ↦
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \mapsto K^\bullet(X)
            turns out to share many properties of the assignment of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            groups
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \mapsto H^n(X,\mathbb{Z})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology
            theory. As such it is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brown+representability+theorem"} represented
            by a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = \mathbb{C}
            this is called
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KU"} KU
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = \mathbb{R}
            this is called
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KO"} KO
            = succeed "-theory.)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KR"} KR
          %p
            One of the basic facts about topological K-theory, rather unexpected from the definition, is that these higher K-groups repeat
            %em periodically
            in the degree
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = \mathbb{R}
            the periodicity is 8, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = \mathbb{C}
            it is 2. This is called
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bott+periodicity"} Bott periodicity
          %p
            It turns out that an important source of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/virtual+vector+bundles"} virtual vector bundles
            representing classes in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
            are
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index+bundles"} index bundles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"} Riemannian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \to B
            called the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+bundle"} spin bundle
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+operator"} differential operator
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operator"} Dirac operator
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index+of+a+Dirac+operator"} index of a Dirac operator
            is the formal difference of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
            by its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernel"} cokernel
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ker
                    %mi D
                    %mo ,
                    %mi coker
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [ker D, coker D]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi D
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D_x
            of Dirac operators/Fredholm operators, parameterized by some topological space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X)
          %p
            It is via this construction that topological K-theory connects to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+geometry"} spin geometry
            (see e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karoubi+K-theory"} Karoubi K-theory
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/index+theory"} index theory
          %p
            As the terminology indicates, both
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+geometry"} spin geometry
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operator"} Dirac operator
            originate in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+physics"} mathematical physics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin%5Ec+quantization"}> spin^c quantization
            ”) in the theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            (where it models
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charge"} D-brane charge
            and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-fields"} RR-fields
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+compactification"} Kaluza-Klein compactification
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+triples"} spectral triples
            (see below).
          %p
            All these geometric constructions have an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+algebra"} operator algebraic
            incarnation: by the topological
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serre-Swan+theorem"} Serre-Swan theorem
            then
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundles"} vector bundles
            of finite rank are equivalently
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebra"} C*-algebra
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
            on the base space. Using this relation one may express K-theory classes entirely operator algebraically, this is called
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+K-theory"} operator K-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirac+operators"} Dirac operators
            are generalized to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fredholm+operators"} Fredholm operators
          %p
            There are more
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebras"} C*-algebras
            than arising as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+of+functions"} algebras of functions
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %em
              \-algebras. One may think of these as defining
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-commutative+geometry"} non-commutative geometry
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+K-theory"} operator K-theory
              immediately generalizes to this situation (see also at
              = succeed ")." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-theory"} KK-theory
          %p
            While the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%2A-algebra"} C*-algebra
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+manifold"} Riemannian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+structure"} spin
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            remembers only the underlying
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+structure"} smooth structure
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemannian+structure"} Riemannian structure
            by passing from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fredholm+modules"} Fredholm modules
            to “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+triples"}> spectral triples
            ”. This may for instance be used to algebraically encode the spin physics underlying the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+K-theory"} operator K-theory
            plays a crucial role in this.
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %p
            The following discussion of topological K-theory in terms of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point-set+topology"} point-set topology
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Snaith%27s+theorem"} Snaith's theorem
            and other pointers at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory"} K-theory
          %p Assumed background for the following is the content of
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundles"} topological vector bundles
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group+of+a+commutative+monoid"} Grothendieck group of a commutative monoid
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+spaces"} pointed topological spaces
          %p
            Throughout, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+field"} topological field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            or the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
          %p In the following we take
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
                to mean
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+space"} finite dimensional vector space
                over
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
                to mean
                = succeed "." do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundle"} topological vector bundle
                    over
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                    of finite
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank+of+a+vector+bundle"} rank
          %p
            We say
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semigroup"} semigroup
                with
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitality"} unit
          %p
            For the most part below we will invoke the assumption that the base
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+space"} compact Hausdorff space
          #DirectSumHasInverseUpToTrivialBundle.num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              %strong
                (over a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+space"} compact Hausdorff space
                every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundle"} topological vector bundle
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum+of+vector+bundles"} direct summand
                of a
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+vector+bundle"} trivial vector bundle
            %p
              For every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundle"} topological vector bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to X
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+Hausdorff+space"} compact Hausdorff space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              there exists a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundle"} topological vector bundle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde E \to X
              such that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum+of+vector+bundles"} direct sum of vector bundles
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E \oplus_X \tilde E \simeq X \times \mathbb{R}^{n}
            %p
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+vector+bundle"} trivial vector bundle
          %p
            For
            %strong proof
            see
            %a{:href => "topological+vector+bundle#TopologicalVectorbundleOverCompactHausdorffSpaceIsDirectSummandOfTrivialBundle"} this prop.
            at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundle"} topological vector bundle
          %h3#the_kgroup The K-group
          %p
            The starting point is the simple observation that the operation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum+of+vector+bundles"} direct sum of vector bundles
            yields a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
            structure (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-group"} semi-group
            with
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitality"} unit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundles"} topological vector bundles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+elements"} inverse elements
            and hence is not an actual
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
          #SemigroupOfIsomorphismClassesOfTopologicalVectorBundlesOnX.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundles"} topological vector bundles
                on
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo ∼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Vect(X)_{/\sim}
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundles"} topological vector bundles
              over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum+of+vector+bundles"} direct sum of vector bundles
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (-)\oplus_X (-)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    Vect(X) \times Vect(X)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    Vect(X)
            %p
              descends to this
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
              by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [E_1] + [E_2]
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    [E_1 \oplus_X E_2]
            %p
              to yield the structure of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-group"} semi-group
              with
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitality"} unit
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi Vect
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mo ∼
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left(
                    Vect(X)_{/\sim}, +
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The operation of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum+of+vector+bundles"} direct sum of vector bundles
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
              in def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SemigroupOfIsomorphismClassesOfTopologicalVectorBundlesOnX"}
              is indeed not a
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              be a chosen point of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              and write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi rk
                      %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo ∼
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    rk_x
                    \\;\colon\;
                    Vect(X)_{/\sim}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\mathbb{N}
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
              which takes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundle"} topological vector bundle
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank+of+a+vector+bundle"} rank
              over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+component"} connected component
              of the point
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            %p
              Then under
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum+of+vector+bundles"} direct sum of vector bundles
              the rank is additive
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi rk
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi rk
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi rk
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    rk_x(E_1 \oplus_X E_2)
                    \\,=\,
                    rk_x(E_1) + rk_x(E_1)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now since the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
              under
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/addition"} addition
              are just a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-group"} semi-group
              with
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitality"} unit
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+element"} inverse element
              under the additive operation, it follows immediately that a necessary condition for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+class"} isomorphism class
              of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundle"} topological vector bundle
              to be invertible under
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum+of+vector+bundles"} direct sum of vector bundles
              is that its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank+of+a+vector+bundle"} rank of a vector bundle
              be zero. But there is only one such class of vector bundles, in fact there is only one such vector bundle, namely the unique rank-zero bundle
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi k
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times k^0
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+vector+bundle"} trivial vector bundle
            %p
              Now for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{N},+)
              it is a time honored fact that it is interesting and useful to rectify its failure of being a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
              by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+construction"} universally
              forcing it to become one. This is a process called
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+completion"} group completion
              and the group completion of the natural numbers is the additive group of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{Z},+)
            %p
              The idea is hence to apply group completion also to the monoid
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Vect
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mo ∼
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Vect(X)_{/\sim}, +)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank+of+a+vector+bundle"} rank
              operation above becomes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+groups"} abelian groups
          %p
            An explicit construction of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+completion"} group completion
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid"} commutative monoid
            is called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group+of+a+commutative+monoid"} Grothendieck group of a commutative monoid
          #KGroupByGrothendieckGroup.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (K-group as the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group+of+a+commutative+monoid"} Grothendieck group
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
                of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundles"} topological vector bundles
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo ∼
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    K(X) \;\coloneqq\; K(Vect(X)_{/\sim}, +)
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+group+of+a+commutative+monoid"} Grothendieck group
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+monoid"} commutative monoid
              (abelian
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-group"} semi-group
              with
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitality"} unit
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundles"} topological vector bundles
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              from def.
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SemigroupOfIsomorphismClassesOfTopologicalVectorBundlesOnX"}
            %p
              This means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
              whose elements are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+classes"} equivalence classes
              of pairs
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo ∼
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mo ∼
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ([E_+], [E_-]) \; \in Vect(X)_{/\sim} \times Vect(X)_{/\sim}
            %p
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism+classes"} isomorphism classes
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundles"} topological vector bundles
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+relation"} equivalence relation
            #eq:DefiningEquivalenceRelation.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi E
                        %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∼
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mo +
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mo −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %mo ∃
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi Vect
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mo ∼
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msub
                            %mi E
                            %mo +
                          %msub
                            %mo ⊕
                            %mi X
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msub
                            %mi E
                            %mo −
                          %msub
                            %mo ⊕
                            %mi X
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msub
                            %mi F
                            %mo +
                          %msub
                            %mo ⊕
                            %mi X
                          %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msub
                            %mi F
                            %mo −
                          %msub
                            %mo ⊕
                            %mi X
                          %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo )
                        %mo )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big(
                    \\left(
                    [E_+], [E_-]
                    \\right)
                    \\;\sim\;
                    \\left(
                    [F_+, F_-]
                    \\right)
                    \\big)
                    \\;\Leftrightarrow\;
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{[G],[H] \in Vect(X)_{/\sim}}{\exists}
                    \\left(
                    \\left([E_+ \oplus_X G] , [E_- \oplus_X G]\right)
                    \\,=\,
                    \\left([F_+ \oplus_X H] , [F_- \oplus_X H]\right)
                    \\right)
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              Here a pair
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ([E_+], [E_-])
              is also called a
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/virtual+vector+bundle"} virtual vector bundle
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [E_+] - [E_-] \;\;\in K(X)
                    \\,.
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+space"} pointed topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              then the difference of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank+of+a+vector+bundle"} ranks
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi rk
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} rk_x(-)
              of the representing vector bundles over the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+component"} connected component
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi rk
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi rk
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi rk
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi E
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    rk_x( [E_+] - [E_-] )
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    rk_x(E_+) -  rk_x(E_-) \in \mathbb{Z}
            %p
              is called the
              %em virtual rank
              of the virtual vector bundle.
          #KGroupOfThePoint.num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              %strong
                (K-group of the point is the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = \ast
              be the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundle"} topological vector bundle
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is just a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Vect
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
