                    E - rk_x(E) &amp;\overset{\phantom{AAAA}}{\mapsto}&amp; (h-1) \tilde \boxtimes (E - rk_x(E))
                    }
            %p is the isomorphism to be established.
          %h3#GradedRingStructure Graded-commutative ring structure
          %p
            The external product on reduced K-groups from prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ExternalTensorProductOnReducedKGroups"}
            allows to extend the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            structure from the plain K-groups (remark
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KTheoryRing"}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GradedKGroups"}
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ProductOnGradedKGroups"}
            below.
          %p To state this definition, recall that
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+topological+space"} pointed topological space
                then the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal"} diagonal
                map to its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product topological space
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times X
                induced a diagonal to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi X
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∨
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \wedge X = (X \times X)/(X \vee X)
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi X
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi q
                      %mi X
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      X \overset{\Delta_X}{\longrightarrow} X \times X \overset{q}{\longrightarrow} X\wedge X
            %li
              %p
                since
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+suspension"} reduced suspension
                is equivalently
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smash+product"} smash product
                with the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                        %mi X
                        %mo ≃
                        %msup
                          %mi S
