                  \\,.
          %p
            %a{:href => "#JackowskiOliver"} Jackowski-Oliver
          %h3#AsAGeneralizedCohomologyTheory As a generalized cohomology theory
          %p
            Topological K-theory satisfies the axioms of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology+theory"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#AtiyahHirzebruch61"}> Atiyah-Hirzebruch 61, 1.8
            ).
          %p
            This is essentially the statement of the long exact sequences
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ExactSequences"} above
          %h3#ComplexOrientationAndFormalGroupLaw Complex orientation and formal group law
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+cohomology+theory"} multiplicative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+%28Eilenberg-Steenrod%29+cohomology"} generalized (Eilenberg-Steenrod) cohomology
            theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+oriented+cohomology"} complex orientable
            if the element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ∈
