          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p
            The “ring of complex vector bundles”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X)
            was introduced in
          %ul
            %li#AtiyahHirzebruch61
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M.+F.+Atiyah"}> M. F. Atiyah
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F.+Hirzebruch"} F. Hirzebruch
              = succeed "," do
                %em Riemann-Roch theorems for differentiable manifolds
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.bams/1183523205"} euclid:bams/1183523205
          %p
            and shown to give a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead-generalized+cohomology"} Whitehead-generalized cohomology
            theory in
          %ul
            %li#AtiyahHirzebruch61
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M.+F.+Atiyah"}> M. F. Atiyah
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F.+Hirzebruch"} F. Hirzebruch
              = succeed "," do
                %em Vector bundles and homogeneous spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %strong III
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9789814401319_0008"} doi:10.1142/9789814401319_0008
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://hirzebruch.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/87/"} web
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=0139181"} MR 0139181
          %p Early lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li#Atiyah67
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em K-theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/atiyahk.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/AtiyahKTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Raoul+Bott"}> Raoul Bott
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Lectures on
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(X)
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/bottk.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Bott-KTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %p
                Russian transl. by B. Yu. Sternin, Matematika
                %strong 11
                2 (1967) 32–56 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.mathnet.ru/eng/mat424"}> mathnet:mat424
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p and further review:
          %ul
            %li#Atiyah69
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Algebraic Topology and Operators in Hilbert Space
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lectures in Modern Analysis and Applications I
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 103
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0099987"} doi:10.1007/BFb0099987
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://webhomes.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/atiyah002.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Atiyah-AlgTopAndOperators.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p Representable K-theory over non-compact spaces was considered in
          %ul
            %li#Karoubi70
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Karoubi"}> Max Karoubi
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Espaces Classifiants en K-Théorie
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/1995218"} jstor
          %p
            and (over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+spaces"} classifying spaces
            in the context of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant K-theory
          %ul
            %li#SegalAtiyah69
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Graeme+Segal"}> Graeme Segal
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"} Michael Atiyah
              = succeed "," do
                %em Equivariant K-theory and completion
              %strong 3
              (1969) 1-18 &amp;lbrack;MR 0259946&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Early lecture notes on topological K-theory in a general context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology+theory"} generalized cohomology theory
            includes
          %ul
            %li#Adams74
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Adams"}> Frank Adams
              , part III, section 2 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stable+homotopy+and+generalised+homology"} Stable homotopy and generalised homology
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li#ConnerFloyd66
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Conner"}> Pierre Conner
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edwin+Floyd"} Edwin Floyd
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Relation+of+Cobordism+to+K-Theories"} The Relation of Cobordism to K-Theories
                %strong 28
                Springer 1966 (
                %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/BFb0071091"}> doi:10.1007/BFb0071091
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/mathscinet-getitem?mr=216511"} MR216511
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (in view of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/U-bordism+theory"} U-bordism theory
                  and the
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/e-invariant"} e-invariant
            %li#Switzer75
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Switzer"}> Robert Switzer
                , sections 11 and 13.90 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic Topology - Homotopy and Homology
                %strong 212
                Springer (1975) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-61923-6_12"}> doi:10.1007/978-3-642-61923-6_12
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Karoubi
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Karoubi"}> Max Karoubi
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em K-Theory – An Introduction
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 226
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://webusers.imj-prg.fr/~max.karoubi/K.book/MK.book.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007%2F978-3-540-79890-3"} doi:10.1007%2F978-3-540-79890-3
            %li#Hatcher
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Allen+Hatcher"}> Allen Hatcher
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Vector bundles and K-theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/VBKT/VBpage.html"} web
            %li#TamakiKono06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dai+Tamaki"}> Dai Tamaki
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Akira+Kono"} Akira Kono
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Generalized Cohomology
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/mmono-230"} ISBN: 978-0-8218-3514-2
          %p Further introductions:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/H.+Blaine+Lawson"}> H. Blaine Lawson
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marie-Louise+Michelsohn"} Marie-Louise Michelsohn
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Spin+geometry"} Spin geometry
            %li#AGP02
              %p
                Marcelo Aguilar,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samuel+Gitler"} Samuel Gitler
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic topology from a homotopical viewpoint
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://tocs.ulb.tu-darmstadt.de/106999419.pdf"} toc pdf
            %li#Courtney04
              %p
                Dennis Courtney,
                %em A brief glance atK-theory
                (2004) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://math.berkeley.edu/~hutching/teach/215b-2004/courtney.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Karoubi06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Karoubi"}> Max Karoubi
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em K-theory. An elementary introduction
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0602082"} arXiv:math/0602082
            %li#Friedlander
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eric+Friedlander"}> Eric Friedlander
                \:
                %em An introduction to K-theory
                (2007) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://users.ictp.it/~pub_off/lectures/lns023/Friedlander/Friedlander.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (focus on
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+K-theory"} algebraic K-theory
            %li#Karpova09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Varvara+Karpova"}> Varvara Karpova
                \:
                %em Complex topological K-theory
                (2009) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://infoscience.epfl.ch/record/162450/files/karpova.semestre.hess2.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/KarpovaTopologicalKTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Blair09
              %p
                Chris Blair:
                %em Some K-theory examples
                (2009) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.maths.tcd.ie/~cblair/notes/kex.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Ioannis P. Zois:
                %em 18 Lectures on K-Theory
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1008.1346"}> arXiv:1008.1346
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Wirthmuller12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Wirthm%C3%BCller"}> Klaus Wirthmüller
                \:
                %em Vector bundles and K-theory
                (2012) &amp;lbrack;
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/wirthmueller-vector-bundles-and-k-theory.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Aderemi Kuku:
                %em Introduction to K-theory and some applications
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.math.ksu.edu/~zlin/kuku/Intro-Kthy.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            A textbook account of topological K-theory with an eye towards
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+K-theory"} operator K-theory
            is section 1 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bruce+Blackadar"}> Bruce Blackadar
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-Theory+for+Operator+Algebras"} K-Theory for Operator Algebras
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comparison+map+between+algebraic+and+topological+K-theory"} comparison map between algebraic and topological K-theory
            is discussed for instance in
          %ul
            %li#Paluch
              %p
                Michael Paluch,
                %em
                  Algebraic
                  = succeed "-theory" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi K
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                K-theory 0471 (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0471/"}> web
                )
            %li#Rosenberg
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jonathan+Rosenberg"}> Jonathan Rosenberg
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Comparison Between Algebraic and Topological K-Theory for Banach Algebras and
                    = succeed "-Algebras" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi C
                              %mo *
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^*
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www2.math.umd.edu/~jmr/algtopK.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            Discussion from the point of view of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+stacks"} smooth stacks
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+K-theory"} differential K-theory
            is in
          %ul
            %li#BunkeNikolausVoelkl13
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ulrich+Bunke"}> Ulrich Bunke
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"} Thomas Nikolaus
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+V%C3%B6lkl"} Michael Völkl
              = succeed "," do
                %em Differential cohomology theories as sheaves of spectra
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1311.3188"} arXiv:1311.3188
          %p
            The proof of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+invariant+one"} Hopf invariant one
            theorem in terms of topological K-theory is due to
          %ul
            %li#AdamsAtiyah66
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Adams"}> Frank Adams
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"} Michael Atiyah
              = succeed "," do
                %em K-theory and the Hopf invariant
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~aar/papers/adamatiy.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+rings"} Hopf rings
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+homology"} ordinary homology
            of topological K-theories:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neil+Strickland"}> Neil Strickland
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Bott periodicity and Hopf rings
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://neil-strickland.staff.shef.ac.uk/research/thesis.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/StricklandHopfRings.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %h3#for_noncompact_spaces_2 For non-compact spaces
          %p
